WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Earlier benchmark: 5× Astra, 7× Opus rounded.
Jev + OpenRouter Qwen; 6 attempts/route, 3 synthetic native tasks.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Your host observes the page and checks the actual result.
Browser Bolt chooses an action or writes field text.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Choose a provider route. Add keys in your local host,
outside this website.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Direct Cerebras uses two provider keys.
Its route is distinct from OpenRouter.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The OpenRouter route uses one key.
Follow the reference host guide for setup.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Copy the configuration.
Copying does not connect your host.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Goals, selected page context and action history
can go to your provider.

8
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Start with synthetic data. Your host executes each action
and checks the actual result.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Four separate live routes. One synthetic checkout per route.
Recorded sequentially, aligned at the first visible fixture.

10
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Original capture speed. Clocks measure time from the first visible frame.
The initial blank frame was omitted.

11
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Task time includes browser setup and verification;
it excludes starting the CLI/MCP process. All four verified.

12
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:18.000
API cost per checkout. OpenRouter reported; Cerebras Qwen estimated.
Hosting, service overhead, support and payment costs excluded.

13
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Get the code. https://github.com/valente-labs/browser-bolt
Setup guide: docs/HOST.md. Start with synthetic data.
